### (a) The byte-literal escape list for `'c'`

- **RECOMMENDATION:**
  - **Byte literal (`'c'`) escapes:** exactly the 6-member closed set `\n` (`0x0a`), `\t` (`0x09`), `\r` (`0x0d`), `\0` (`0x00`), `\\` (`0x5c`), `\'` (`0x27`).
  - **`\"` in `'c'`:** **Refused** (write `'"'`).
  - **`\'` in `"..."`:** **Refused** (write `'`). String literal (`"..."`) escapes remain the 6-member closed set `\n`, `\t`, `\r`, `\0`, `\\`, `\"`.
  - **`\xHH`:** **Refused** in both byte literals and string literals. Non-printable bytes outside `\n`, `\t`, `\r`, `\0` are written as integer literals (e.g. `0x1b` or `0x1bu8`, or `27u8`).
- **ALTERNATIVE:**
  - Unify both literal kinds to a single 7-member escape list (`\n`, `\t`, `\r`, `\0`, `\\`, `\'`, `\"`), or add `\xHH` to `'c'` for non-printable ASCII control bytes.
- **REASONS:**
  - **One form per situation ([docs/PHILOSOPHY.md:54-57](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L54-L57)):** Inside `'...'`, the raw double quote `'"'` requires no delimiter escaping; allowing `'\"'` creates two spellings (`'"'` and `'\"'`) for byte `0x22`. Likewise, inside `"..."`, raw `'` is unambiguous and `\'` is already omitted in [legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:428](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#L428) (SYN-5) and [docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:113-114](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L113-L114).
  - **No `\xHH` duplication ([OWNER_29_DECISIONS_2026-11-08.md:12](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/OWNER_29_DECISIONS_2026-11-08.md#L12)):** Item 3 decides that `'a'` has type `u8` (`'a'` == `97u8`). Because a byte literal is already a `u8` expression, adding `'\x1b'` would merely duplicate the integer literal `0x1bu8` (or `0x1b` in a `u8`-expected context). In strings, `\xHH` is already refused by SYN-5 ([legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:443-444](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#L443-L444)) so that static text is guaranteed valid UTF-8 ([docs/decisions.md:233](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/decisions.md#L233) Core Q4.2, [docs/decisions.md:1417](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/decisions.md#L1417) OD127).
  - Matches the exact 6-member list in SYN-6 ([legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:456](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#L456)) and OPEN-6 ([docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:113-116](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L113-L116), [632](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L632)).
- **CONFLICTS WITH DECIDED ROWS:**
  - None. Note that **Item 3** ([OWNER_29_DECISIONS_2026-11-08.md:12](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/OWNER_29_DECISIONS_2026-11-08.md#L12)) explicitly revises language item 16 (removing `char` and giving `'a'` type `u8`), so the legacy `char` references in [docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:88](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L88), [100](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L100), [114-116](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L114-L116), [legacy/docs/spec/types.md:1403-1420](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/legacy/docs/spec/types.md#L1403-L1420) (TYPE-20), and [docs/decisions.md:1332](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/decisions.md#L1332) (OD42) are superseded by Item 3's revision.

