### (b) The exact control-character set refused raw inside strings, byte literals, and comments

- **RECOMMENDATION:**
  - **Inside byte literals (`'c'`):**
    - Refuse all raw bytes outside `U+0020..=U+007E` (i.e. refuse raw C0 controls `U+0000..=U+001F`, including raw HT `U+0009`, LF `U+000A`, CR `U+000D`, plus DEL `U+007F`, and all non-ASCII `>= U+0080`), as well as raw `'` (`U+0027`) and `\` (`U+005C`).
    - Thus, a raw unescaped character in `'c'` is strictly in `U+0020..=U+0026 | U+0028..=U+005B | U+005D..=U+007E`.
  - **Inside string literals (`"..."`) AND line comments (`// ...`):**
    - Refuse all raw Unicode control, line/paragraph separator, and bidirectional formatting scalars, specified as the exact closed union of code-point ranges:
      1. `U+0000..=U+001F` (C0 controls — **including raw HT `U+0009`, raw LF `U+000A`, and raw CR `U+000D`**: multiline raw strings are refused; write `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0`),
      2. `U+007F..=U+009F` (DEL and C1 controls; thus all of Unicode general category `Cc`),
      3. `U+2028..=U+2029` (Unicode Line Separator and Paragraph Separator),
      4. `U+061C`, `U+200E..=U+200F`, `U+202A..=U+202E`, `U+2066..=U+2069` (Unicode bidirectional control characters: ALM, LRM, RLM, LRE, RLE, PDF, LRO, RLO, LRI, RLI, FSI, PDI).
    - (In `//` line comments, raw HT `U+0009` may be permitted only if source trivia allows tabs per Foundation Q10 [docs/decisions.md:1083-1085](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/decisions.md#L1083-L1085), or refused alongside all other controls except the line-terminating LF `U+000A` / CR `U+000D`; all other ranges above — `U+0000..=U+0008`, `U+000B..=U+000C`, `U+000E..=U+001F`, `U+007F..=U+009F`, `U+2028..=U+2029`, and the bidi controls `U+061C`, `U+200E..=U+200F`, `U+202A..=U+202E`, `U+2066..=U+2069` — must be refused in comments as well.)
- **ALTERNATIVE:**
  - Refuse only ASCII controls `U+0000..=U+001F` and `U+007F` in strings and byte literals (leaving C1 `U+0080..=U+009F`, `U+2028..=U+2029`, and bidi controls permitted in UTF-8 strings and comments).
- **REASONS:**
  - **Transparency and hostile-input auditability ([docs/PHILOSOPHY.md:59-61](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L59-L61) Rule 3, [235-239](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L235-L239) AT 13):** Bidi controls (`U+061C`, `U+200E..=U+200F`, `U+202A..=U+202E`, `U+2066..=U+2069`) are the vector for "Trojan Source" attacks (CVE-2021-42574), where source text or a comment visually reorders tokens so a human auditor sees different logic than the compiler parses. `U+2028..=U+2029` cause line-ending desynchronization between editors/tools and the lexer (splitting a `//` comment visually across lines while the lexer treats it as still commented). C1 controls (`U+0080..=U+009F`) are invisible non-printable characters in UTF-8 that can spoof terminal output or hide payload bytes in string literals.
  - **One form & platform-independent bytes ([docs/PHILOSOPHY.md:54-57](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L54-L57) Rule 2, [legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:439-440](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#L439-L440) SYN-5):** Refusing raw LF (`U+000A`) and raw CR (`U+000D`) inside string literals prevents two ways to write a newline (raw newline vs `\n`) and eliminates silent byte changes (`0x0a` vs `0x0d 0x0a`) when git or an editor converts line endings. This matches OPEN-6 ([docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:632](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/proposals/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md#L632)) and Item 4 ([OWNER_29_DECISIONS_2026-11-08.md:13](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/OWNER_29_DECISIONS_2026-11-08.md#L13)).
  - **Simple Lean judgment ([docs/PHILOSOPHY.md:208-209](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#L208-L209) AT 4):** Stating the forbidden set as explicit code-point interval predicates in Lean requires no external Unicode database dependency in `ConcreteSpec`.
- **CONFLICTS WITH DECIDED ROWS:**
  - None. Core Q4.2 ([docs/decisions.md:233](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/round-lexspell/src/docs/decisions.md#L233), "UTF-8 including embedded NUL") is satisfied via the escape `\0`, while raw NUL (`U+0000`) is refused in source and literals.

